    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FitzGerald's are delighted to present this charming 19th Century cottage in the picturesque village of Gowran for sale by private treaty.   The property which was built in 1864 forms part of a row of similar cottages situated on Main Street.   The cottage is ideally located at the end of the row. Part of the property contained within the garden is unregistered and is being sold “as is”. Purchasers are advised that the vendor is selling the house and their interest only in the unregistered adjoining land. The vendor will provide a certificate of long use and procession of this land to the purchaser. \r\n\r\nThe property is laid out over two floors, ground floor accommodation comprises an entrance porch, open plan kitchen living room, dining room and extension to the back which incorporates a bathroom.  First floor accommodation has two bedrooms. \r\n  \r\nWhile the property is need of total refurbishment it offers enormous potential to create a charming first home, holiday home or investment opportunity. This is a very quaint property with lots of character and charm.    \r\n\r\nThe property has been vacant for over two years and may qualify for the Vacant Properties Refurbishment Grant.  \r\n\r\nThis property is a unique opportunity for buyers to purchase a delightful property full of potential. \r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended.   \r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION \r\n\r\nGROUND FLOOR\r\nENTRANCE PORCH\t \r\nKITCHEN & SITTING ROOM \t3.3m x 4.2m\twith solid fuel range and staircase to first floor.\r\nDINING ROOM / BEDROOM \t        2.4m x 4.3m\t\r\nBACK HALL\t\t                        2.3m x 1.0m\twith door leading to garden. \r\nBATHROOM\t\t                        2.3m x 1.6m\twith wc, whb and shower. \r\nFIRST FLOOR\r\nBEDROOM 1\t\t                \t3.1m x 4.2m\twith velux window and original solid fuel fireplace. \r\nBEDROOM 2\t\t\t                3.2m x 4.2m \twith velux window. \r\n\r\nSERVICES\t\r\nElectricity, mains water supply, mains sewage, single glazed timber windows."
      },
